{{!-- The add-a-person bar under a standing roster: brands, oaths, and the Blessed's marks.

      The other half of roster-row.hbs, and here for the same reason. All three lists add the same
      way — free-type a name against a datalist of world actors, press the button, or drop an Actor
      on the section — and the block had been written out three times across two files with the
      class stem swapped, including the five-line note about `label` vs `value` pasted verbatim
      twice. A fourth roster (marked-people.js and RosterDialog both anticipate one) would have
      been a fourth copy.

      Free-type rather than a picker because the person very often has no Actor at all: a Censure
      lands on somebody nobody has made a document for, a Proclamation's faction never has one, a
      ward names a doorway and a Shared Souls beast is usually just a beast. A typed name that
      matches an actor exactly is stored as a link to them anyway (see RosterDialog `_addTyped`),
      so typing and dropping record the same thing.

      Anything a particular list picks BEFORE the name — the Blessed's kind chooser — goes in the
      block body, which renders at the head of the bar. A caller with nothing to add invokes it
      with an empty block.

      Context:
        prefix       class stem for the shared chrome ("stonetop-condemned", "stonetop-marks")
        nameClass    the text input's class, which the host dialog reads the typed name from
        listId       id tying the input to its datalist; unique per bar on the page
        addClass     the add button's class, which the host binds its click to
        addLabel     that button's label, already localized
        placeholder  the input's placeholder, already localized
        hint         the "or drop an actor here" line, already localized
        suggestions  {value, hint} rows for the datalist --}}
<div class="{{prefix}}-add">
	{{> @partial-block}}
	<input type="text" class="{{nameClass}}" list="{{listId}}"
	       autocomplete="off" placeholder="{{placeholder}}">
	{{!-- `label` is where a native datalist already means "the aside beside this option", and it
	      is what StonetopAutocomplete renders as the dimmed second column. Only `value` is ever
	      inserted into the field, so a picked "Brennan the Claw / Marshedge" types just the name
	      and the search resolves it cleanly. --}}
	<datalist id="{{listId}}">
		{{#each suggestions}}<option value="{{value}}"{{#if hint}} label="{{hint}}"{{/if}}></option>{{/each}}
	</datalist>
	<button type="button" class="{{addClass}}">{{addLabel}}</button>
</div>
<p class="{{prefix}}-hint">{{hint}}</p>
